{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/tbl-knot-operator-basis-table-table1-data","@type":["folio-assistant-core:Table","doco:Table"],"label":"tbl:knot-operator-basis-table-table1-data","kind":"table","title":"Data table 1 from rem:knot-operator-basis-table","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/rem-knot-operator-basis-table"],"tags":["extracted-table"],"text":"knot-operator-basis-table-table1-data.md","provenance":"authored","html":"<p><a id=\"tbl:knot-operator-basis-table-table1-data\"></a>\n<strong>Table.</strong> <em>Data table 1 from rem:knot-operator-basis-table</em></p>\n<p><strong>Table L.1 — normal-form (NF) basis multiplication.</strong> This table\nrecords the raw product <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">b_i \\cdot b_j</code> of the NF basis operators —\nthe case of the identity operator <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\beta(T_{1,0}) = \\mathbf{1}</code> —\nre-expanded in the same basis. Reading the row <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">b_i</code> against the\ncolumn <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">b_j</code> gives the coefficient of that column operator in the\nproduct <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">b_i \\cdot b_j</code>; every entry is exact in <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">h</code>, and \"—\" marks a\nvanishing coefficient.</p>\n<p><strong>Notation.</strong> <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">h = q - q^{-1}</code> (Hecke amplitude). The NF basis is\n<code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\{\\ \\gamma,\\ \\sigma_0,\\ \\sigma_1,\\ L_+,\\ L_-,\\ e^-\\ \\}</code>, with\n<code class=\"language-math math-inline\">e^- = \\sigma_0\\sigma_1\\sigma_0</code> (the trefoil). The operator <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\gamma</code>\nis the two-sided identity: <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\gamma \\cdot b_j = b_j</code> and\n<code class=\"language-math math-inline\">b_i \\cdot \\gamma = b_i</code>. The identity rows below (the header row\n<code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\gamma \\cdot b_j</code> and the right-multiply rows <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">b_i \\cdot \\gamma</code>)\ntherefore list the single surviving operator directly and leave the\nremaining cells empty.</p>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th align=\"left\"><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">b_i \\cdot b_j</code></th>\n<th align=\"center\"><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\gamma</code></th>\n<th align=\"center\"><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\sigma_0</code></th>\n<th align=\"center\"><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\sigma_1</code></th>\n<th align=\"center\"><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">L_+</code></th>\n<th align=\"center\"><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">L_-</code></th>\n<th align=\"center\"><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">e^-</code></th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"left\"><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\gamma \\cdot b_j</code></td>\n<td align=\"center\"><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\gamma</code></td>\n<td align=\"center\"><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\sigma_0</code></td>\n<td align=\"center\"><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\sigma_1</code></td>\n<td align=\"center\"><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">L_+</code></td>\n<td align=\"center\"><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">L_-</code></td>\n<td align=\"center\"><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">e^-</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"left\"><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\sigma_0 \\cdot \\gamma</code></td>\n<td align=\"center\"><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\sigma_0</code></td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"left\"><code class=\"langua